\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Jesus, the very thought of  Thee
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 With sweetness fills the breast;
\par But sweeter for Thy face to see,
\par And in Thy presence rest.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  O Hope of every contrite heart,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 O Joy of all the meek,
\par To those who ask how kind Thou art,
\par How good to those who seek.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.  But what to those who find? Ah! this
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Nor tongue nor pen can show;
\par The love of Jesus, what it is
\par None but His loved ones know
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  Jesus, our only Joy be Thou,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 As Thou our prize will be;
\par In Thee be all our glory now,
\par And through eternity.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

